        "market_heading": "Why home staging matters in the San Diego market",
        "market_text": "<p>San Diego's steady stream of military and defense-industry relocations means a constant pool of buyers shopping on short timelines from far away — buyers who rank listings almost entirely by photos before a whirlwind house-hunting trip. Home staging gets a listing shortlisted; empty photos get skipped.</p><p>And like the rest of coastal California, the lifestyle is the pitch: staged patios, decks and indoor-outdoor rooms let a La Jolla condo or a North Park bungalow sell the weather along with the walls.</p><p>The ADU boom adds a second job for staging here. A converted garage or granny flat is often the reason a buyer stretches for the property, but photographed empty it reads as storage. Staged as a studio with a bed, a table and a place to sit, it reads as the rental income or in-law suite the listing is really selling.</p>",
